From c5752c5ce477674d4f25c3627f03204cea8da8fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: simply0001 <nicolas.tobago@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 02:25:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 35/50] [video_core/macro] keep all macro code in one shared
 buffer

Every macro upload got its own heap vector inside a map, and calling into the middle of a blob copied the whole tail into yet another vector before compiling, where the std::move doesn't save the allocation since dynamically sized vectors can't elide the heap. Now all uploaded words land in a single append-only vector and each method just records a start/size pair into it, so a mid-method call becomes a plain offset entry with no copy at all. Spans are only materialized at the point of use, because a stored span would dangle whenever the shared vector grows on append.

The interpreter also copied its parameters into a member vector on every execution; it now reads the caller's span directly, which is the same contract the JIT always had. Macro upload bursts used to go word by word through CallMethod, paying the shadow RAM check, the dirty table stores and the method switch per word, so CallMultiMethod now handles load_mme.instruction in bulk like const_buffer and inline_data already do. ProcessMacroUpload is gone since nothing calls it and its instruction_ptr++ contradicted the live upload path.

Also fixes the dump suffix, the decompiled flag was always true so LLE macros were dumped with the jit label.

Continues the macro work from #4236.

(cherry picked from commit ac0279684f29fbd91fbb7d824b9edb319970762b)
